{
  "name": "Allowly SEAL - Managed webhook JSON evidence",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## One private URL, one Allowly node\n1. Open **SEAL** in Allowly and copy the private webhook URL.\n2. Create an **Allowly SEAL Webhook** credential in n8n and paste the URL there.\n3. Attach that credential to **2. SEAL + WAIT + VERIFY**.\n4. Map your JSON and optional Type, Reference, and Statement in step 1, then execute.\n\nNo API key or policy setup is needed. Treat the private URL like a password. Receipt details are stored in the signed receipt; they are not extracted from the JSON. A sealed result includes a verified signature and matching record. A pending result is shown with a safe attempt ID and is never archived as sealed evidence.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 520
      },
      "id": "0d7d89f0-1bd1-5fb6-ac45-15e339f5ea8e",
      "name": "SETUP - Private webhook URL",
